<phrase>
  id: LANG_SOLITAIRE_HELP_AIM
  desc: in Solitaire's Help, the first paragraph: the aim and the rules. Menu is the iPod's Menu button, named as the iPod's manual in your language names it
  user: extras
  <source>
    *: "Move all the cards onto the four piles at the top right, each by suit from ace to king. In the seven columns, put each card on one a rank higher and of the other colour; only a king goes into an empty column. Menu turns over cards from the deck at the top left, one or three at a time as set in Draw Cards."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "Viige kõik kaardid paremal üleval olevale neljale virnale, igaüks oma masti kaupa ässast kuningani. Seitsmes veerus pange iga kaart ühe võrra kõrgemale ja teist värvi kaardile; tühja veergu sobib ainult kuningas. Menu pöörab kaarte vasakul üleval olevast pakist, ühe või kolm korraga, nagu on määratud seadega „Kaartide pööramine“."
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
<phrase>
  id: LANG_SOLITAIRE_HELP_MOVE
  desc: in Solitaire's Help, the second paragraph: moving the cursor. ◀ and ▶ are the iPod's Previous and Next buttons, kept as these signs; the wheel is the click wheel
  user: extras
  <source>
    *: "◀ and ▶ move between the columns; past the first or the last one, they go to the turned card beside the deck. The wheel moves up and down a column, and along the top row between the turned card and the four piles."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "◀ ja ▶ liiguvad veergude vahel; esimesest või viimasest edasi lähevad need paki kõrval olevale pööratud kaardile. Ratas liigub veerus üles ja alla ning ülemises reas pööratud kaardi ja nelja virna vahel."
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
<phrase>
  id: LANG_SOLITAIRE_HELP_SELECT
  desc: in Solitaire's Help, the third paragraph: moving cards. Select and Menu are the iPod's buttons of those names, as the iPod's manual in your language names them
  user: extras
  <source>
    *: "Select picks up the card under the cursor. Select on another column or pile moves it there with the cards on it, or puts it back if it can't go there. Select on the same card again sends it to its pile if it fits. Menu also puts back a card picked up."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "Select võtab kursori all oleva kaardi üles. Select teisel veerul või virnal viib selle koos peal olevate kaartidega sinna või paneb tagasi, kui see sinna ei sobi. Select uuesti samal kaardil saadab selle oma virnale, kui see sobib. Ka Menu paneb ülesvõetud kaardi tagasi."
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
<phrase>
  id: LANG_SOLITAIRE_HELP_SHORTCUTS
  desc: in Solitaire's Help, the last paragraph: the buttons held. Play, Menu and Select are the iPod's buttons, ▶ its Next button kept as this sign; the turned card is the face-up card beside the deck at the top left
  user: extras
  <source>
    *: "Play puts the turned card where the cursor is. Hold ▶ to send the turned card to its pile, or hold Menu to send the card under the cursor to its pile. Hold Select for the menu."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "Play paneb pööratud kaardi kursori kohale. Hoidke all nuppu ▶, et saata pööratud kaart oma virnale, või hoidke all nuppu Menu, et saata kursori all olev kaart oma virnale. Menüü avamiseks hoidke all nuppu Select."
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
